        "tool_use_id": "call_c4b337f27c4343e1b8cb801e",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "# Project Handoffs MCP Server\n\n**Description:** An MCP tool for aiding persistence over AI coding agent sessions.\n\n## What It Does\n\nThis is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that provides tools for managing AI session handoffs and tracking next steps across coding sessions. It helps maintain continuity when AI agents work on projects over multiple sessions.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n- Implements a workflow chain of NextStep → WorkingSession → Handoff → New NextStep\n- Organizes work by projects\n- Uses priority levels to indicate implementation impact:\n  - core-critical: essential for working implementation\n  - full-required: necessary for desired implementation  \n  - enhancement: improvements and optimizations\n\n## Available Tools\n\n- `list_templates` - view templates for next steps, sessions, and handoffs\n- `create_project` - start a new project tracking workspace\n- `delete_project` - remove a project and its data\n- `create_next_step` - add new tasks to a project\n- `start_working_session` - begin work on a specific next step\n- `create_handoff` - complete a session with handoff documentation\n- `get_latest_next_steps` - retrieve open tasks ordered by priority\n- `get_next_step_history` - view complete history of a task\n\n## Installation & Setup\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build\n```\n\nConfigure by adding to MCP settings with the node command path and the build/index.js file path.\n\n## Technical Features\n\nThe implementation includes error handling through a ProjectError class, template validation for all entity types, consistent state management, and safe data persistence following project-memory-server patterns. Licensed under Apache License 2.0."
      }
    ]
  },
