        "content": "# OpenAI CodeAgent-action Overview\n\n**Description**: A GitHub Action that \"invokes openAI API as GenAI agent and coding in pipeline offline.\"\n\n## What It Does\n\nThis tool enables developers to integrate large language models into CI/CD workflows without requiring fine-tuning or RAG. By constructing specific instructions for pipeline tasks, it provides intelligent solutions to enhance production efficiency.\n\n## Core Approach\n\nThe project focuses on gathering sufficient context and building targeted prompts that can be sent directly to LLMs, avoiding the complexity of retrieval-augmented generation or model training.\n\n## Key Features\n\n| Category | Tools | Language | Scenario |\n|----------|-------|----------|----------|\n| Unit Test | Jest | JavaScript | Auto-generate unit tests to improve coverage |\n| Doc Gen | - | Go | Generate GoDoc comments via AST analysis |\n| CVE Scan with Pod security | Syft, Bomber | deployment.yaml | Detect CVEs and suggest Pod Security Policy improvements |\n| CVE Scan with project | Syft, Bomber | n/A | Detect CVEs and their impact on your repository |\n| Code Vulnerabilities Scan | - | C | Detect common CVE patterns such as null pointer issues |\n\n## Technical Architecture\n\nThe action employs AST (Abstract Syntax Tree) analysis combined with prompt engineering. It supports multiple scanning types including static analysis, CVE detection, and OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities through a pluggable interface design.\n\n## Current Results\n\nThe documentation notes confirmed outcomes including \"3 confrimed CVE upgrade from a cloud related project\" and \"submit one PR to an Apache project.\"\n\n## Usage Methods\n\nUsers can run the action via containers with environment variables for API configuration, or generate output locally and review results through a provided UI interface."
