        "content": "# ai.nvim\n\n**Description:** \"AI stuff in neovim\"\n\n## Overview\n\nThis is a Neovim plugin that integrates AI functionality directly into the editor. Currently marked as work in progress, with support for Google's Gemini AI model.\n\n## Main Features\n\n**Quick Change Mode:**\n- Use `:AiSuggestion` in normal or visual mode\n- Opens a floating prompt window\n- AI-generated content replaces selected text upon pressing enter\n\n**Chat Interface:**\n- Use `:AiChat` command to open a split window\n- Conversational interface with messages prefixed by `User:`\n- Supports file references using `@file:<file path>` syntax\n- Can reference the current file with `@file:current`\n- Included files become part of the system prompt\n\n## Installation\n\nDesigned for use with lazy.nvim plugin manager. Requires a Google AI API key stored in a local file. Users can configure custom keymaps (example shows `<M-k>` binding).\n\n## Developer Value\n\nProvides AI-assisted text editing and code generation without leaving Neovim. Enables conversational AI interactions with project context through file references. The plugin aims to support different scope levels (file, selection, or codebase) in future versions.\n\nThe repository includes sample conversations and is openly licensed."
