        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "Based on the GitHub repository content, here's what I extracted:\n\n## **AI-CallConnect Overview**\n\n**AI-CallConnect** is an AI-powered phone agent designed for \"seamless voice interactions, dynamic data handling, and scalable communication.\" It targets modern sales and customer engagement solutions.\n\n## **Key Features**\n\n### Voice Integration\n- **Speech-to-Text**: Converts user voice input into text\n- **Text-to-Speech**: Generates voice responses from the AI agent\n\n### Core Technical Components\n1. **Data Processing**: Uses the Switchboard Dialog Dataset with artificial dataset augmentation\n2. **Matching Algorithms**: Implements fuzzy matching and exact matching for query handling\n3. **Text Processing**: Leverages NLTK for cleaning and preprocessing dialogues\n4. **Voice System**: Powered by SpeechRecognition, pyttsx3, and gTTS libraries\n\n## **What It Does for Developers**\n\nThe tool provides developers with a complete framework for building voice-enabled conversational agents. It handles the complex pipeline from voice input → text processing → pattern matching → response generation → voice output.\n\nTwo deployment modes exist:\n- **Local version** (`streamlit_app_local.py`): Full voice input/output support\n- **Deployed version** (`streamlit_app.py`): Text-only due to Streamlit server limitations with system audio dependencies\n\n## **Technical Stack**\n- **Frontend**: Streamlit web application framework\n- **Data Processing**: Pandas for dataset manipulation\n- **NLP**: NLTK for text preprocessing\n- **Audio**: PyAudio, Pygame for audio handling\n- **Matching**: Fuzzywuzzy for text similarity matching\n\n## **Architecture**\n\nThe system follows a pipeline approach: Dataset → Cleaning & Preprocessing → Exploratory Data Analysis → Matching Algorithms → Streamlit Application Interface with voice capabilities."
      }
    ]
  },
